# Copy this file to .env (same folder) and fill in what you have. Never commit the real .env (it is git-ignored).
# EVERYTHING here is optional: with no keys at all the app runs fully on local data (the ticker says OFFLINE_FALLBACK, vessels are SIMULATED,
# news is classified by rules). Keys stay on the server; the browser never sees them. Real values go only in .env, never in this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- price (WTI / Brent ticker)
# Free EIA Open Data key. Register at https://www.eia.gov/opendata/register.php
# Without it the ticker shows the last row of data/oil_daily_prices.csv, labelled OFFLINE_FALLBACK.
EIA_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- tanker feed
# AISStream.io key (free, sign in with GitHub at https://aisstream.io). Without it the globe shows SIMULATED vessels.
# The AIS adapter is UNVERIFIED against the live feed until someone runs it with a real key.
AISSTREAM_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- older news-classification pipeline (backend/news/)
# Anthropic key: lets that pipeline classify headlines with Claude. Without it a rule-based classifier is used.
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# NewsAPI key for that pipeline's polling. NOTE: NewsAPI's free Developer plan is for development and testing only, not production.
# Without it the pipeline runs on fixtures only. Register at https://newsapi.org/register
NEWSAPI_API_KEY=

# Seconds between NewsAPI polls. Unset = 1200 (20 min) = 72 calls a day, under the free plan's 100/day.
# NEWS_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- route news (GDELT, no key needed)
# Fill the route-news cache at startup, one route at a time. Unset = on (1), 0 = off (cold-start measurements, offline work).
# The test suite sets it to 0.
# NEWS_WARMUP=

# Seconds between startup warm-up fetches (unset = 6) and the minimum gap between any two GDELT requests (default 6). GDELT answers HTTP 429 if you go faster.
# NEWS_WARMUP_GAP=
# NEWS_MIN_REQUEST_INTERVAL=

# GDELT endpoint (unset = https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc). Only change it for testing against a stand-in.
# NEWS_GDELT_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ShipFinder AIS (server-side only)
# Key from the ShipFinder Open Platform console (https://open.shipfinder.com). It goes in the request URL as key=..., so it is redacted from every log
# record. Never put the value in this file, in git, or anywhere the browser can read. The key and every service on it expire on 2026-11-13.
AIS_API_KEY=

# Kill switch. 0 stops every provider call (the app falls back to saved snapshots, then to simulated vessels). Unset = on (1).
# AIS_ENABLED=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- DEV ONLY: do not set these in a real deployment
# Point the price feed at the dev-only mock EIA server (tools/mock_eia_server.py), e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8765/v2 and 1. BOTH must be set, otherwise EIA_BASE_URL is ignored and the
# real EIA API is used. The price source is then labelled "DEV STAND-IN for EIA (NOT EIA DATA)".
# EIA_BASE_URL=
# PRICE_DEV_ALLOW_CUSTOM_EIA_URL=

# Testing only: pretend today is this date (YYYY-MM-DD) to check the expired-key behaviour without waiting for 2026-11-13. Leave empty in normal use.
# AIS_TODAY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- HOSTED MODE (a public deployment, M16)
# Nothing below is secret and none of it needs a value to run locally. Unset = the default described on each line. Local mode (HOSTED_MODE unset) changes nothing.
#
# 1 = public deployment: visitors are served from caches filled by one scheduled refresh a day (no visitor ever causes an EIA or GDELT call), rate limits are on,
# developer endpoints are closed, CORS allows only FRONTEND_ORIGIN, and every source below follows its own flag. Unset or 0 = local.
# HOSTED_MODE=
#
# One flag per source, read only when HOSTED_MODE=1. 1 = allowed, 0 = off. The defaults are the safe side:
#   ON by default : EIA, GDELT, TRADINGVIEW, GEM, ANTHROPIC (capped, see CLAUDE_* below)
#   OFF by default: SHIPFINDER (hosted shows SIMULATED vessels only), AISSTREAM (not set up), NEWSAPI, ALPHAVANTAGE,
#                   SHIPFINDER_DISTANCES (hosted uses the earlier estimated voyage distances)
# HOSTED_ENABLE_EIA=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_GDELT=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_TRADINGVIEW=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_GEM=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_ANTHROPIC=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_SHIPFINDER=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_AISSTREAM=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_NEWSAPI=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_ALPHAVANTAGE=
# HOSTED_ENABLE_SHIPFINDER_DISTANCES=

# The ONE web address allowed to call this API from a browser in hosted mode, e.g. https://your-site.example (no trailing path). Unset = no cross-origin caller.
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=

# Link shown in the footer. Unset = the project's public repository.
# PUBLIC_REPO_URL=

# Hours between scheduled refreshes in hosted mode. Unset = 24.
# REFRESH_INTERVAL_HOURS=

# Claude classifier limits (hosted and local): each headline is classified once and cached; after the daily call cap or the monthly dollar cap the rule-based
# classifier answers instead. Unset = 50 calls a day and 5.00 dollars a month. The prices per million tokens are an ASSUMPTION (unset = 5 in, 25 out, the highest
# of the model family, so the cap stops early rather than late). CLAUDE_CLASSIFIER_MODEL unset = the model named in news/classifier_claude.py.
# CLAUDE_DAILY_CALL_CAP=
# CLAUDE_MONTHLY_USD_CAP=
# CLAUDE_INPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=
# CLAUDE_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=
# CLAUDE_CLASSIFIER_MODEL=
